TITLE:: SwarmSynthDefs
SUMMARY:: Reusable sine-partial SynthDef builders
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>SwarmSynth
RELATED:: Classes/SwarmMath, Classes/SwarmSynth

DESCRIPTION::
Builds the standard sine partial, sustained, pad, and chip graphs used with
SwarmSynth. Builders return SynthDef objects without registering them or
starting a server. Call code::.add:: on a returned definition, or use
code::install:: for the canonical library names.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: partial
Builds an attack/decay or gate-sustained sine partial. The code::nyquistMode::
control is passed directly to code::SwarmMath.frequencyPolicy::.

ARGUMENT:: name
SynthDef name.

METHOD:: sustained
Builds a gate-controlled sine voice with pulse, saw, amplitude, detune, phase,
pan, and Nyquist-policy modulation.

ARGUMENT:: name
SynthDef name.

ARGUMENT:: gateBeforeAmp
When false, controls begin code::out, freq, amp, fadeTime, gate::. When true,
they begin code::out, freq, gate, amp, fadeTime::. The alternate order exists
for compatibility with compositions whose SynthDef contract already uses it;
the UGen graph is otherwise identical. Defaults to false.

METHOD:: pad
Builds a self-freeing sine pad with a linen envelope and detune modulation.

ARGUMENT:: name
SynthDef name.

METHOD:: chip
Builds a self-freeing sine chip voice. Legacy folding is enabled by default and
is applied after detuning.

ARGUMENT:: name
SynthDef name.

METHOD:: install
Registers code::swarm_partial::, code::swarm_sustained::, code::swarm_pad::,
and code::swarm_chip:: in SynthDescLib and sends them to running servers using
SynthDef's normal code::.add:: behavior. It does not boot a server.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Construction alone is inert.
~voiceDefinition = SwarmSynthDefs.sustained(\mySustainedVoice);

// Register only the definition needed by the composition.
~voiceDefinition.add;
~voice = SwarmSynth.new(\mySustainedVoice);

// Or install all canonical definitions explicitly.
SwarmSynthDefs.install;
::
